Z||000008||stimpy||06-10-2001||03:41 PM||||Hehe, no, that's powdercoat. The red is for the EGR covers I got.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712481&Sequence=5"> <BR>The yellar on the heatsheilds and the vent tubes is DupliColor Daytona Yellow. Really good paint.<p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||CoolBlue87GT||06-10-2001||04:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierokid87:<BR><B>WOW  that looks awesome!  Is that the crysler red?  also, how did you ger the silver parts to look so good?<P>Scott</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I guess you haven't seen my car yet. That<BR>is the stock paint from the factory on the<BR>engine !!  I've used "Liquid Glass" wax to<BR>polish it up a bit.<BR>.<BR>It was taken 'bout a month ago.  You see,<BR>the car only has 1700 miles !!  I've owned<BR>the car since new.<BR>.<BR>That's how it looks as you say, "so awesome"<BR>.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBlue87GT.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000010||Galen||06-10-2001||05:02 PM||||Can I ask a question? why buy a car if you're not gonna drive it? the designers didn't design the car to be looked at .. they designed it to be driven. Not drivin a car is a waste in my opinion. Even if it is a fiero. Its still a waste of a car.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierokid87||06-11-2001||11:58 AM||||Hey guys thats so much for the suggested color!  It looks awesome.  Now how do I get the silver loovers back?<P>Scott||||reg||10
Z||000012||CoolBlue87GT||06-11-2001||11:58 AM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>why buy a car if you're not gonna drive it. Not drivin a car is a waste in my opinion<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Those that know me (used to be Fierodave87gt) understand my story, and accept it.<P>Of course I am usually a calm down to earth person, and add usefull posts and have met / made many friends here and at many car shows.<P>I've owned Fiero's starting w/ an 84 4cyl, then 85 SE V6. Bought both brand new, and totaly enjoyed them to the max. Drove them everywhere and combined logged 'bout 250+k.<P>When I ordered the 87 (in SEP 1986), I knew it was going to be a keeper. With the color blue and GT V6 compo and the rest of the options that I choose I knew was going to be a rare Fiero.<P>My decision to keep the miles low were not without pain, but it was <B> my </B> decision. I love the car enough to keep it the best way I can. I've spent hours detailing it and enjoying it the way I want.<P>Please do not make fun of me for doing that. I felt as if I needed to defend myself for keeping the miles low.<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBlue87GT.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 06-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||06-11-2001||12:27 PM||||Ouch! I don't think Galen came anywhere close to flaming you. If he had said "Only a (pick your own perjoritive) would buy a car and never drive it.", yeah that would qualify as a flame job. But just stating his opinion that he thinks it's a waste not to drive a car, well, you might be a bit thin skinned about that.  Of course it is a waste. In th strictest sense, any luxury is a waste. But if you can afford to maintain this luxury, more power to you. It's a beautiful car and you are justifiably proud of it. But it is like having nice living room furniture that you never sit on. Kinda defeats the purpose.<P>Oh, and Fierokid, metal polish, soft cottn rags and LOTS of elbow grease will clean up the aluminum. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Alex4mula||06-11-2001||12:33 PM||||This is Factory paint too. 88 Formula with 169456 miles. Chevy orange-red engine paint is very close too.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p8cd6608274de9501de9b32aa3e00ec24/fe6d7726.jpg.orig.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||JSocha||06-11-2001||12:41 PM||||HEY!  My 87 GT has a tad over 65K on it and I'm not driving it...<P>perhaps thats because its still in the service shop.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Anyways, I only drive my Fiero for pleasure, otherwise it is parked in my heated/AC garage.  If I find an 88 GT w/T-Tops with well under 15K miles (or less then 1K which I prefer) on it for the right price, it is going to be garaged and only taken out on very rare occassions and trailered to long distance events.<P>If I would have bought the PPE or the following car (if it hadn't been bid to an outrageous price) <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=592095418&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=592095418&r=0&t=0</A>  , I guarantee that either one of these cars would have been put in storage, cared for and maintaned and be lucky to see 50 miles in a 5 month period.<P>Why?  Just because they are rare to find low milage, vintage stock vehicles (not including the modified 86 on Ebay or the PPE).  <P>When the rest of you are putting on the 200K, others will have a vehicle deemed more then its weight in gold to us enthusiasts.  I feel coolblue did the right thing.<P>Just my .02.  Now I have to go find two more pennies outside so I break even again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||CoolBlue87GT||06-11-2001||01:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Ouch! well, you might be a bit thin skinned about that.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've toned down that message, - reread.<P>The last car show I drove it to (Daytona), many people had options,  most said they would not drive it, and trailer it to shows far away.<P>The first/next show I trailered it to was Carlise PA.  When one of the first people that I spoke to at the show, heard it was not driven, and they were quick to call it a "Trailer Queen".<P>Now most people told me to trailer it, then to have fun made of it ? I took that in stride, (did hurt a little). <P>This comment hurt also. Have thought about it for awhile now and yes, I was to quick to post my comment.  <P>As I read in another post, measure twice, cut once.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fierokid87||06-11-2001||01:23 PM||||Ok guys lets stick to the subject of the original post.  I posted this for those who want to have thier V-6's look good again.  Now what I ment is how do you take the paint off the loovers when you have repainted the valve covers and plenum.  Oh and dont flame me.  I just want to stick to the original subject.  Those of you who dont drive your Fieros everyday more power to you.  Makes your Fieros more special with low milage and all.  Those who drive them alot.  that means you love your cars in a different way then those who dont drive them as much.  We are all Fiero freaks.  <P>Scott||||reg||3
